{% comment %}
  A centred statement: eyebrow, heading, one paragraph of argument.

  Covers the mockup's .centerintro (light) and .statement (navy). They differ
  only in surface, so this is one section with a `dark` toggle.

  RATION THE DARK VARIANT. It is a full-bleed band, and the design allows few
  per page -- a tier-2 hero and the closing CTA are usually dark already. A
  third flattens the page's rhythm rather than adding emphasis.

  The dark variant supplies its own vertical rhythm through margin-block, so it
  does NOT take .suf-section. A full-bleed band cannot pad itself from inside a
  section wrapper without the background stopping short.

  ELEMENT. The root is a <div>: `"tag": "section"` already wraps this.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign classes = 'suf-statement'
  if section.settings.dark
    assign classes = classes | append: ' suf-statement--dark'
  else
    assign classes = 'suf-section ' | append: classes
    # Only on the light variant. The dark one is a full-bleed band that does
    # not carry .suf-section, so it has no section padding to drop.
    if section.settings.intro
      assign classes = classes | append: ' suf-section--flush-bottom'
    endif
  endif
  assign anchor = section.settings.anchor | handle
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The anchor belongs on the INTRO, not on the thing it introduces.

  This section is often the heading above a list or grid -- "Upcoming
  Seminars", "Seminar Schedule". A link that targets the list lands the reader
  mid-content with the heading scrolled off above it, so they arrive without
  the label that tells them what they are looking at.

  The scroll offset is handled positionally in _suf-components.scss, so this
  works on the dark variant too, which does not carry .suf-section.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="{{ classes }}" {% if anchor != blank %}id="{{ anchor }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="suf-wrap">
    {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
      <p class="suf-eyebrow">{% render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.eyebrow %}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h2>{% render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.heading %}</h2>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
      <div class="suf-statement__body">{% render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.body %}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Statement (SUF)",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "anchor",
      "label": "Anchor id",
      "info": "Lets a link elsewhere jump here, e.g. \"upcoming\". Put it on the intro rather than on the list below it, so the reader lands on the heading."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow"
    },
    {
      "type": "inline_richtext",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "body",
      "label": "Body",
      "info": "Italicise at most one phrase -- on the dark variant it renders as the highlight, and a second stops it reading as emphasis."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "dark",
      "label": "Dark band",
      "info": "Full-bleed navy. Count the dark bands already on the page before adding another.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "intro",
      "label": "Introduces the section below",
      "info": "Drops the gap underneath so this reads as the heading for what follows. Light variant only.",
      "default": false
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Statement (SUF)"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
